WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.647 --> 00:00:08.048
Frank and Lisa were visiting their grandparents.

2
00:00:08.068 --> 00:00:11.110
"Get dressed and come down to breakfast.

3
00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:16.533
Also, find your bathing suits because we'll be swimming at the lake," said Mom.

4
00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:20.835
Frank couldn't find his bathing suit.

5
00:00:22.456 --> 00:00:26.318
"Mom told you to pack your bathing suit," scolded Lisa.

6
00:00:26.338 --> 00:00:29.280
"I guess you won't be going swimming today."

7
00:00:30.188 --> 00:00:31.208
"Be quiet!"

8
00:00:31.688 --> 00:00:32.369
said Frank.

9
00:00:32.389 --> 00:00:37.590
"I can wear my shorts to swim, as long as I bring an extra pair."

10
00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.191
"Lisa! Frank!

11
00:00:41.611 --> 00:00:45.132
Your breakfast is getting cold," called their grandma.

12
00:00:45.152 --> 00:00:47.433
"We're coming!"

13
00:00:47.813 --> 00:00:48.673
answered Lisa.

14
00:00:48.693 --> 00:00:50.834
"Found it!"

15
00:00:51.274 --> 00:00:52.854
shouted Frank happily.

16
00:00:56.915 --> 00:00:59.416
Frank, this room is a mess!

17
00:01:00.048 --> 00:01:02.369
Why are all your clothes on the floor?"

18
00:01:02.869 --> 00:01:03.549
asked Mom.

19
00:01:03.569 --> 00:01:08.350
"He couldn't find his bathing suit," said Lisa.

20
00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:15.332
"Frank, you must put your clothes away before you have breakfast," said Mom.

21
00:01:15.352 --> 00:01:19.173
"Yes, Mom," answered Frank.

22
00:01:23.455 --> 00:01:25.695
many pancakes can you eat?"

23
00:01:26.115 --> 00:01:27.736
asked Grandma at breakfast.

24
00:01:28.908 --> 00:01:31.230
"I can eat three," said Lisa.

25
00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:33.613
"Do you have maple syrup?"

26
00:01:34.554 --> 00:01:36.475
"Yes," replied Grandpa.

27
00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:37.697
"It's real.

28
00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:39.338
I made it this spring."

29
00:01:39.358 --> 00:01:41.981
"You made it?

30
00:01:42.401 --> 00:01:44.343
How?" asked Lisa.

31
00:01:44.363 --> 00:01:48.286
"Well, it takes a lot of work.

32
00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:53.832
But each spring, as the weather gets warmer, the sap begins to run in the maple trees."

33
00:01:56.196 --> 00:01:59.978
"Sap?" asked Lisa with a mouthful of pancakes.

34
00:01:59.998 --> 00:02:03.961
"Sap is tree blood," said Grandpa.

35
00:02:03.981 --> 00:02:08.023
"Yuck," said Lisa.

36
00:02:08.043 --> 00:02:11.605
"Syrup is made from blood!"

37
00:02:11.625 --> 00:02:15.847
"Lisa, tree blood isn't like human blood.

38
00:02:16.207 --> 00:02:19.649
Tree blood, sap, is mostly water and sugar.

39
00:02:20.129 --> 00:02:24.932
After a long winter's nap, a tree needs a nice long drink of sweet water.

40
00:02:25.412 --> 00:02:30.754
In the spring I take some of the sweet water from the maple trees and make maple syrup."

41
00:02:34.576 --> 00:02:36.517
there any pancakes left for me?"

42
00:02:36.997 --> 00:02:37.697
asked Frank.

43
00:02:39.398 --> 00:02:41.298
"Sure, there's plenty.

44
00:02:41.719 --> 00:02:43.379
How many can you eat?"

45
00:02:43.739 --> 00:02:44.620
asked Grandma.

46
00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.421
"I can eat three," said Frank.

47
00:02:47.441 --> 00:02:49.062
"Pass the syrup, please."

48
00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:54.744
Dad?" asked Frank.

49
00:02:56.116 --> 00:03:00.677
"Oh, he took the boat to the lake this morning to go fishing," answered Mom.

50
00:03:01.698 --> 00:03:04.298
"Really?" said Frank sadly.

51
00:03:04.318 --> 00:03:06.699
"Why didn't he take me?"

52
00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:14.261
"Because he got up really early, before the sun came up," said Grandma.

53
00:03:14.281 --> 00:03:17.402
"Here, have some fruit."

54
00:03:18.822 --> 00:03:21.243
"I want an apple," said Lisa.

55
00:03:21.263 --> 00:03:23.504
"Can I have a banana?"

56
00:03:23.884 --> 00:03:24.624
asked Frank.

57
00:03:25.908 --> 00:03:27.630
"Ouch! My tooth!"

58
00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:28.871
cried Lisa.

59
00:03:28.891 --> 00:03:31.033
"What's wrong?"

60
00:03:31.353 --> 00:03:32.094
asked Mom.

61
00:03:32.114 --> 00:03:34.516
"My, my tooth.

62
00:03:34.976 --> 00:03:35.757
It's loose.

63
00:03:37.058 --> 00:03:39.200
Will I have to go to the dentist?

64
00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.842
Will I miss our trip to the lake?"

65
00:03:42.323 --> 00:03:43.123
asked Lisa.

66
00:03:43.143 --> 00:03:46.987
"Lisa, calm down," said Mom.

67
00:03:47.007 --> 00:03:52.752
"Lisa, you're a big girl now," said Grandma.

68
00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.821
"A big girl because I have a cavity."

69
00:03:56.841 --> 00:04:01.202
"You don't have a cavity," said Mom, laughing.

70
00:04:01.222 --> 00:04:03.543
"You have a loose tooth."

71
00:04:03.563 --> 00:04:12.845
"Today," continued Grandma, "you're a big girl because you're losing your baby teeth."

72
00:04:14.906 --> 00:04:16.847
"I'm losing my teeth?"

73
00:04:17.227 --> 00:04:19.107
asked Lisa, very concerned.

74
00:04:19.127 --> 00:04:26.379
"Yes," said Mom, "but new, bigger teeth will grow in place of the ones you lose."

75
00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:33.224
"Your mother lost her teeth when she was your age," said Grandma.

76
00:04:33.244 --> 00:04:36.346
"Really?" asked Lisa.

77
00:04:36.366 --> 00:04:39.788
"Yes, really," said Grandpa.

78
00:04:39.808 --> 00:04:43.691
"But the best thing about losing your teeth is the tooth fairy."

79
00:04:43.711 --> 00:04:46.513
"The tooth fairy?"

80
00:04:47.013 --> 00:04:47.834
asked Lisa.

81
00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:53.653
"Yes, when your tooth falls out, you take it and place it under your pillow.

82
00:04:54.073 --> 00:04:57.254
While you are sleeping, the tooth fairy will take the tooth.

83
00:04:57.655 --> 00:05:02.116
In exchange, the tooth fairy will grant you one wish," said Grandpa.

84
00:05:02.136 --> 00:05:04.978
"When can I make a wish?

85
00:05:05.378 --> 00:05:07.359
When will my tooth fall out?"

86
00:05:07.739 --> 00:05:08.579
asked Lisa.

87
00:05:08.599 --> 00:05:10.880
"Maybe today.

88
00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.441
Maybe tomorrow," said Mom.

89
00:05:14.281 --> 00:05:17.543
"You can't rush nature," said Grandma.

90
00:05:17.563 --> 00:05:20.344
"It will come out when it's ready."
